1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:02,085
[WOMAN] <i>We love it!</i>

2
00:00:02,168 --> 00:00:03,002
<i>Oh, thank you.</i>

3
00:00:03,086 --> 00:00:04,671
[WOMAN] <i>We still need one more approval.</i>

4
00:00:04,754 --> 00:00:05,922
<i>Billy, Jordan,</i>

5
00:00:06,005 --> 00:00:08,383
<i>I'd like you to meet Mr. Alvin Ramirez.</i>

6
00:00:08,466 --> 00:00:10,468
<i>Do we really have to do this, dude?</i>

7
00:00:10,552 --> 00:00:12,887
<i>Once LoveList becomes successful,</i>

8
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:14,723
<i>even Oliver will benefit from it.</i>

9
00:00:14,806 --> 00:00:18,977
<i>And think about the women</i>
<i>at Angels of Grace.</i>

10
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:21,855
[MULTIPLE PHONES CHIMING]

11
00:00:21,938 --> 00:00:24,274
<i>Alvin! You better stop signing that.</i>

12
00:00:24,357 --> 00:00:25,233
<i>Gia?</i>

13
00:00:25,316 --> 00:00:26,443
<i>- Let's go!</i>
<i>- What's going on?</i>

14
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:28,153
<i>- What's happening?</i>
- [GIA GRUNTS]

15
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:31,322
[ALVIN] <i>You know, Billy, trying</i>
<i>to reconnect with you was a mistake.</i>

16
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:32,782
<i>Deal is off.</i>

17
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:34,576
[TONI] <i>Who would even do this?</i>

18
00:00:34,659 --> 00:00:36,161
[MARJ] <i>It has to be Valerie.</i>

19
00:00:36,244 --> 00:00:38,371
<i>Did you have anything to do with</i>
<i>LoveList getting hacked?</i>

20
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:40,540
<i>Am I the only person with</i>
<i>a grudge against you?</i>

21
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:41,666
- [VALERIE GROANS]
<i>- Ma'am!</i>

22
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:44,919
- [WOMAN]<i> Ma'am!</i>
- [VALERIE CRYING]

23
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:47,589
You shouldn't have hit Val.

24
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:51,926
After everything she said
about me and my family?

25
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:53,720
Do you think I'd just let it slide?

26
00:00:57,557 --> 00:01:03,772
[ENGINE MISFIRING]

27
00:01:03,855 --> 00:01:05,231
What's wrong?

28
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:07,859
Let me do it.

29
00:01:10,862 --> 00:01:11,780
Relax.

30
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:14,240
[GRUNTS]

31
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:16,409
[ENGINE MISFIRES]

32
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:17,952
It's probably an engine problem.

33
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:21,081
I think you'll have to get it fixed
at the auto repair shop.

34
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:26,628
[SCREAMS, GRUNTS]

35
00:01:26,711 --> 00:01:27,629
[THUDS]

36
00:01:31,299 --> 00:01:32,175
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

37
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:33,760
Are you done?

38
00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:40,809
- Come on, smile.
- [CLICKS TONGUE]

39
00:01:41,351 --> 00:01:42,393
[JORDAN] Psst.

40
00:01:43,144 --> 00:01:44,020
Stop!

41
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:51,069
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

42
00:02:00,203 --> 00:02:01,538
We're gonna fix this.

43
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:05,375
Trust me.

44
00:02:11,881 --> 00:02:12,799
Hey.

45
00:02:12,882 --> 00:02:18,763
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

46
00:02:26,312 --> 00:02:27,564
Don't worry about your car.

47
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:30,400
We'll pick it up tomorrow.

48
00:02:33,069 --> 00:02:34,529
Just go home for now.

49
00:02:39,826 --> 00:02:40,785
Okay.

50
00:02:43,329 --> 00:02:50,044
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

51
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,834
[BILLY] Do you think
we can track down the hacker?

52
00:03:31,085 --> 00:03:32,045
I can try.

53
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:35,089
Thank you.

54
00:03:37,008 --> 00:03:38,468
Dude!

55
00:03:38,551 --> 00:03:40,803
A shooting star. Did you see it?

56
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:43,097
Make a wish.

57
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:46,935
I can't let a shooting star
decide LoveList's future.

58
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:51,773
Well, unless it invests in us.

59
00:03:52,523 --> 00:03:53,691
That'd be nice.

60
00:03:54,275 --> 00:03:55,109
Impossible.

61
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:58,571
I don't want our efforts to go to waste.

62
00:04:00,281 --> 00:04:03,576
You know, since I already
invested my money,

63
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:05,286
let's just do it.

64
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:08,831
Come hell or high water,
we will launch LoveLine.

65
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:10,291
How?

66
00:04:11,125 --> 00:04:12,293
You no longer have an investor.

67
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:15,296
I'll pawn the house. Double mortgage!

68
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:17,382
- [FLICKS] You're nuts!
- Ow!

69
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:21,552
This is what you need.

70
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:28,393
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

71
00:04:37,151 --> 00:04:38,236
[CHUCKLES]

72
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:43,366
[BILLY] Shooting star,

73
00:04:43,449 --> 00:04:44,617
my wish

74
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:48,454
is that we can catch that darn hacker.

75
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:51,416
Will you grant my wish, shooting star?

76
00:04:51,499 --> 00:04:53,668
Please, shooting star.

77
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:55,753
[IN TINY VOICE] Okay.

78
00:04:58,589 --> 00:05:00,800
Thank you, shooting star.
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

79
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:07,390
[BILLY] Auntie Pres?

80
00:05:08,558 --> 00:05:09,851
[PRECIOUS] Oh, Billy!

81
00:05:09,934 --> 00:05:12,061
Come here. Let's eat.

82
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:14,939
- Hi, Auntie Pres.
- Let's eat.

83
00:05:15,481 --> 00:05:16,482
Oh, where's Oliver?

84
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:18,067
He's already sleeping.

85
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:20,028
Then why are there three plates?

86
00:05:20,111 --> 00:05:21,738
Didn't you see my message?

87
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:23,865
We have a visitor.

88
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:24,991
Who?

89
00:05:25,074 --> 00:05:26,367
[PRECIOUS] Just there.

90
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:28,995
- Come.
- Ms. Billy!

91
00:05:29,078 --> 00:05:30,121
[ABI] Hello!

92
00:05:30,204 --> 00:05:31,164
Abi!

93
00:05:31,247 --> 00:05:34,417
I went to the center earlier.

94
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:36,294
I wanted to thank you

95
00:05:36,377 --> 00:05:40,798
because our conversation
really helped me a lot.

96
00:05:40,882 --> 00:05:43,217
- [BILLY] Mm…
- But you weren't there

97
00:05:43,301 --> 00:05:47,305
so Ms. Precious became
the victim of my endless talking.

98
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:50,058
That's why I brought her with me.

99
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:51,851
- I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

100
00:05:51,934 --> 00:05:54,270
It's okay. You don't have to thank me.

101
00:05:54,353 --> 00:05:58,024
I usually do that, maybe once
a week, at the center.

102
00:05:58,107 --> 00:06:00,068
I like helping people.

103
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:01,819
I'm glad I could help you.

104
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:05,114
Oh, I'm so glad she's my idol.

105
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:07,867
You help a lot of people.

106
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:11,162
But, Ms. Billy, who helps you?

107
00:06:11,245 --> 00:06:14,540
I saw what happened with LoveList.

108
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:16,542
I just got worried,

109
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:19,295
so that's one of the reasons why I'm here.

110
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:21,714
- Mm.
- Also, have you seen this?

111
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:23,091
Here.

112
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:26,886
[VALERIE]<i> Hi, guys.</i>

113
00:06:26,969 --> 00:06:29,555
<i>So Doc Rosie was just here,</i>

114
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:32,975
<i>and, yes, this happened.</i>

115
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:35,770
[WHIMPERS]

116
00:06:35,853 --> 00:06:37,814
<i>It's still a bit swollen right now, guys,</i>

117
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:40,441
<i>but I think it's getting better.</i>

118
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:45,238
<i>I mean, I still look pretty, thank God.</i>

119
00:06:45,321 --> 00:06:48,032
<i>So, yeah.</i>

120
00:06:48,116 --> 00:06:49,867
<i>Long story short, guys,</i>

121
00:06:49,951 --> 00:06:51,369
<i>there was an issue</i>

122
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:55,623
<i>with that deranged CEO</i>
<i>who won't leave me alone!</i>

123
00:06:55,706 --> 00:06:57,583
<i>I didn't even do anything!</i>

124
00:07:00,044 --> 00:07:01,879
You know what, Ms. Billy?

125
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:03,381
I think

126
00:07:03,464 --> 00:07:06,592
she's just messing with you.

127
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:08,594
She wants you to react.

128
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:10,012
And once you do,

129
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:12,014
she'll make content out of it.

130
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:15,601
I've been taking care
of this company for years.

131
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:17,228
I'm not gonna back down now.

132
00:07:17,311 --> 00:07:18,771
- Mm.
- All right.

133
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:21,232
Remember, it's okay to fight back,

134
00:07:21,315 --> 00:07:23,401
but not in that way.

135
00:07:23,985 --> 00:07:25,403
I'm sorry, Auntie Pres.

136
00:07:26,195 --> 00:07:30,032
I'm just mad at people
who can't fight without hiding.

137
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:33,369
I can't just let them get away with this.

138
00:07:33,995 --> 00:07:37,373
The moment I find out
who started all this,

139
00:07:37,457 --> 00:07:40,918
I'll do everything I can
to put them in jail.

140
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:43,004
They don't know
what I'm like when I'm angry.

141
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:47,008
- I'm sorry, Abi.
- [ABI] Hmm?

142
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:49,260
I'm sorry about this.

143
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:52,847
I'm not really good at handling my anger.

144
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:56,767
Oh, Ms. Billy, don't worry about me.

145
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:58,144
I'm perfectly fine.

146
00:07:58,227 --> 00:08:03,065
If I could,
I'd help you in any way possible.

147
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,984
And I mean, anything.

148
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:09,989
Enough of that. Come on and eat.

149
00:08:10,072 --> 00:08:11,991
You haven't even taken a bite.

150
00:08:12,074 --> 00:08:14,035
[PRECIOUS] Keep eating, dear.

151
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:15,620
Come on.

152
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:17,246
Hey.

153
00:08:18,539 --> 00:08:19,499
Okay.

154
00:08:19,582 --> 00:08:25,755
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYS]

155
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:34,096
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

156
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:36,682
Dude.

157
00:08:37,975 --> 00:08:41,103
Thanks again for blocking
the LoveSpeak hacker.

158
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:42,647
[EXHALES] Dude…

159
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:45,399
It's so hard to trace this hacker.

160
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:51,948
They used proxies, cloaked IPs,
layered encryption, everything.

161
00:08:53,866 --> 00:08:55,785
Whoever it was,

162
00:08:55,868 --> 00:08:57,161
they're still not stopping.

163
00:08:57,245 --> 00:09:00,122
People are still reposting the same video.

164
00:09:01,541 --> 00:09:04,085
I think it's the same person.
What do you think?

165
00:09:09,173 --> 00:09:12,843
Aren't these like the troll accounts
we had on LoveSpeak?

166
00:09:13,511 --> 00:09:16,013
- Can you check it out?
- You're right.

167
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:17,390
I noticed too.

168
00:09:18,724 --> 00:09:20,935
Okay. I'll take care of it.

169
00:09:21,936 --> 00:09:23,104
Ah, dude, I'm sorry.

170
00:09:23,187 --> 00:09:26,023
Oliver's Family Day
will be this Saturday, okay?

171
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:27,275
Don't forget about it.

172
00:09:27,358 --> 00:09:29,819
Of course. All right now.
I'll take care of this.

173
00:09:30,444 --> 00:09:31,904
Good night. Thank you.

174
00:09:35,866 --> 00:09:38,911
Sis, it's Family Day tomorrow.
1:00 p.m. sharp.

175
00:09:38,995 --> 00:09:40,871
Yes, sir. I'd never forget.

176
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:42,623
Jordan is coming too.

177
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:44,166
- See you.
- Bye, sis!

178
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:47,295
- I'm gonna miss you!
- Wow! I'll miss you too!

179
00:09:47,378 --> 00:09:48,296
Bye-bye!

180
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:49,547
Take care, mister.

181
00:09:50,298 --> 00:09:51,465
[VAN DOOR CLOSES]

182
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:02,059
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:03,519
Auntie Pres?

184
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:07,148
[PRECIOUS] I'm coming!

185
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:08,899
Yes? What is it?

186
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:11,986
Auntie, did you see
my keys here last night?

187
00:10:12,069 --> 00:10:13,404
Do you know where I put them?

188
00:10:13,487 --> 00:10:14,905
Well, those are mine.

189
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:19,869
Maybe you left them in your car
or at the office?

190
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:20,870
I don't think so.

191
00:10:20,953 --> 00:10:25,166
I remember using them last night
when I opened the door.

192
00:10:25,249 --> 00:10:27,043
You were cooking at the time.

193
00:10:27,918 --> 00:10:29,629
Or… was it already open?

194
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:31,380
I'm sorry, Auntie.

195
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:33,758
- [PRECIOUS] Uh…
- I can't remember.

196
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:35,343
A lot happened last night.

197
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:36,844
All right. Okay, I got it.

198
00:10:36,927 --> 00:10:37,845
Here's what we'll do.

199
00:10:37,928 --> 00:10:39,639
You can use my keys for now,

200
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:41,974
and I'll try to look for yours
when I get home.

201
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:43,392
- Okay?
- Thank you.

202
00:10:43,476 --> 00:10:44,685
- Okay, okay.
- Take care.

203
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:46,854
- Love you.
- Love you!

204
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,773
[PHONE RINGS]

205
00:10:49,815 --> 00:10:51,692
Hello? Dude.

206
00:10:51,776 --> 00:10:53,611
Mission accomplished, dude.

207
00:10:53,694 --> 00:10:54,820
Your wish

208
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:56,364
is my command.

209
00:10:56,447 --> 00:10:57,823
Good news?

210
00:10:59,075 --> 00:11:00,868
This hacker thinks he's a pro.

211
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:02,495
But I'm a lot better.

212
00:11:02,578 --> 00:11:04,372
<i>He tried to log in earlier,</i>

213
00:11:04,455 --> 00:11:07,375
so I sent a fake password reset link.

214
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:10,503
I got his location!

215
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:11,754
Finally!

216
00:11:11,837 --> 00:11:15,132
Mm. Thank you, dude. Thank you.

217
00:11:15,216 --> 00:11:17,468
You're welcome. Anything for you, dude.

218
00:11:19,553 --> 00:11:23,474
Miss, there are no grounds to file a case
based only on your suspicions.

219
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:26,936
If you want, we can file
an incident report instead.

220
00:11:27,019 --> 00:11:30,689
I understand that suspicion
is not enough grounds.

221
00:11:30,773 --> 00:11:32,942
But I've suffered actual damage

222
00:11:33,025 --> 00:11:36,028
to my company, my finances,
and my reputation.

223
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:39,031
We have the location
of the account involved.

224
00:11:39,115 --> 00:11:41,784
They can respond to any question
we may have for them.

225
00:11:44,036 --> 00:11:46,497
Can you trace the troll's identity?

226
00:11:47,289 --> 00:11:49,417
Miss, this is just GPS data.

227
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:52,628
It's not admissible
without a chain of custody.

228
00:11:52,711 --> 00:11:54,713
You will first need
to file a formal complaint

229
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:57,174
in order to obtain a court order.

230
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:59,385
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

231
00:11:59,468 --> 00:12:02,221
How did you get the troll's location?

232
00:12:02,304 --> 00:12:04,473
If you don't have permission,
that's illegal.

233
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:06,434
Sir!

234
00:12:06,517 --> 00:12:10,438
This person hacked the accounts
on our app.

235
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:12,022
Isn't that illegal too?

236
00:12:12,648 --> 00:12:13,983
We know that.

237
00:12:14,066 --> 00:12:16,861
But what you did was
counter-hacking or phishing.

238
00:12:16,944 --> 00:12:18,988
They can sue you too,

239
00:12:19,071 --> 00:12:22,783
under the Cybercrime Law
and Data Policy Act.

240
00:12:22,867 --> 00:12:23,826
That's right.

241
00:12:25,244 --> 00:12:27,705
Are you saying that
there's nothing we can do?

242
00:12:27,788 --> 00:12:30,499
Well, you didn't really do it legally.

243
00:12:30,583 --> 00:12:32,293
And you still don't have proof.

244
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:37,882
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

245
00:12:39,925 --> 00:12:46,098
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

246
00:12:55,316 --> 00:13:00,446
[MUSIC TURNS SUSPENSEFUL]

247
00:13:01,405 --> 00:13:04,074
[CAR LOCKS]

248
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:22,009
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

249
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:25,221
Miss!

250
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:27,139
Where you going?

251
00:13:27,681 --> 00:13:29,099
Bye, beautiful!

252
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:35,898
[CALOY] Yeah.

253
00:13:37,441 --> 00:13:39,443
They can change passwords all they want.

254
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:41,737
She can even block me from her app.

255
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:42,863
I can still hack it, anyway.

256
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:46,700
Just tell me

257
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:49,078
if you want to hack LoveList again.

258
00:13:50,329 --> 00:13:54,166
I can post stuff on
Benilda Cariño's account too.

259
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:58,295
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:13:58,379 --> 00:13:59,380
[CALOY] You want that?

261
00:14:01,215 --> 00:14:02,174
All right.

262
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:07,763
[CALOY MUTTERS INDISTINCTLY]

263
00:14:13,561 --> 00:14:16,355
Boss! B-b-b--Oh, wow.

264
00:14:16,939 --> 00:14:19,483
Bo-- Good morning. Hi.

265
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:22,444
- People are waiting downstairs.
- All right, I'll be there.

266
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:23,654
You sure?

267
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:25,865
- Yeah.
- Can you be there today?

268
00:14:26,490 --> 00:14:27,408
Good morning.

269
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:30,786
[PHONE VIBRATES]

270
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:34,623
- Dude.
- Hello?

271
00:14:36,083 --> 00:14:39,044
Jordan, I've been calling you.

272
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:40,462
Sorry, I fell asleep.

273
00:14:41,297 --> 00:14:44,133
I'm outside the troll's house.

274
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:45,092
<i>What?!</i>

275
00:14:45,175 --> 00:14:47,970
Dude! That's dangerous.

276
00:14:48,053 --> 00:14:49,263
Leave now!

277
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:52,558
The police said they needed proof, right?

278
00:14:52,641 --> 00:14:54,810
<i>Then I'll give them what they want.</i>

279
00:14:55,561 --> 00:14:57,897
Benilda, you're going too far.

280
00:14:57,980 --> 00:14:59,690
<i>If you don't leave there,</i>

281
00:14:59,773 --> 00:15:02,443
I won't be friends with you anymore.

282
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:04,987
- [CALL DROPS]
- Billy.

283
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:06,196
Hello?

284
00:15:06,864 --> 00:15:13,871
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

285
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:35,893
[MUSIC TURNS SUSPENSEFUL]

286
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:39,605
[CALOY CHUCKLING, CRUNCHING SNACKS]

287
00:15:50,866 --> 00:15:56,997
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

288
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:01,085
[CALOY] Hey! Who's there?

289
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:03,253
Who's there?

290
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:05,339
Hey!

291
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:07,174
Miss!

292
00:16:09,301 --> 00:16:12,638
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

293
00:16:12,721 --> 00:16:14,598
[CALOY] Hey! Give that to me.

294
00:16:14,682 --> 00:16:16,266
Delete the picture you took.

295
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:17,518
Give me your phone.

296
00:16:17,601 --> 00:16:19,144
Don't come any closer.

297
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:21,105
I'll scream if you come any closer.

298
00:16:21,188 --> 00:16:23,983
You'll scream? Go ahead. Do it!

299
00:16:24,066 --> 00:16:25,275
I can even help you!

300
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:27,486
- Give me your phone!
- Who were you talking to earlier?

301
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:29,822
Who's giving you these orders?

302
00:16:29,905 --> 00:16:31,156
Why would I tell you?

303
00:16:31,865 --> 00:16:32,908
Huh?

304
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,576
Ms. Benilda Cariño?

305
00:16:35,369 --> 00:16:37,371
Give me your phone.
I'll delete the picture.

306
00:16:37,454 --> 00:16:38,914
Otherwise, you'll only get hurt.

307
00:16:39,623 --> 00:16:40,749
- [YELPS]
- I said give that to me!

308
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:42,001
Get off me!

309
00:16:42,084 --> 00:16:43,627
Help!

310
00:16:44,253 --> 00:16:45,379
[YELPS]

311
00:16:46,672 --> 00:16:48,632
- [GRUNTS]
- That hurt!

312
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:50,926
- Come here!
- Help me, please!

313
00:16:51,927 --> 00:16:53,637
[GROANS]

314
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:54,680
[GRUNTS]

315
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:56,640
- You little…
- [SCREAMS]

316
00:16:56,724 --> 00:16:57,808
Help me, please!

317
00:16:57,891 --> 00:16:59,643
[CRYING]

318
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:01,020
Who are you?!

319
00:17:01,812 --> 00:17:03,397
[GRUNTS]

320
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:07,901
Jordan!

321
00:17:08,485 --> 00:17:10,279
[YELPS]

322
00:17:11,405 --> 00:17:12,364
Ha!

323
00:17:13,032 --> 00:17:14,324
- [CALOY] C'mon!
- Jordan!

324
00:17:15,117 --> 00:17:16,869
- [GRUNTS] Come on!
- Help, please!

325
00:17:17,494 --> 00:17:18,787
Jordan!

326
00:17:19,955 --> 00:17:21,832
[GROANS]

327
00:17:21,915 --> 00:17:23,208
That's enough!

328
00:17:25,419 --> 00:17:27,296
[GRUNTS]

329
00:17:27,379 --> 00:17:28,255
Someone, help us!

330
00:17:28,338 --> 00:17:29,715
[GROANS]

331
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:31,800
- [FLESH RIPS]
- [SCREAMS]

332
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:33,677
Leave!

333
00:17:34,845 --> 00:17:35,679
Well?

334
00:17:35,763 --> 00:17:38,348
[BILLY WHIMPERING, BREATHING HEAVILY]

335
00:17:38,932 --> 00:17:40,100
[GRUNTS]

336
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:42,478
- I told you to leave!
- [BILLY] That's enough!

337
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:44,480
Enough! Jordan, we need to go!

338
00:17:44,563 --> 00:17:45,814
Help!

339
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:49,234
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

340
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:50,903
[OBJECTS CLATTERING]

341
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:53,572
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

342
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:55,783
[DOOR SCRAPING]

343
00:17:58,494 --> 00:17:59,745
[CELL PHONE BEEPING]

344
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:01,914
[LINE RINGING]

345
00:18:02,623 --> 00:18:03,832
Hello?

346
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:05,125
We've got a problem.

347
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:07,544
We've got a problem!

348
00:18:09,963 --> 00:18:12,299
- [PATROLMAN] Hands up! Get down!
- [CALOY] Wait.

349
00:18:12,382 --> 00:18:15,803
- [GRUNTS]
- Stop fighting back!

350
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:22,476
- Slowly! Slowly!
- Hey!

351
00:18:22,559 --> 00:18:23,477
I can do it.

352
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,354
There we go!

353
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:27,606
Does it hurt?

354
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:28,565
I can handle it.

355
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:32,236
You should be thankful
that it's not life-threatening.

356
00:18:32,903 --> 00:18:34,863
You only needed four stitches, but still.

357
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:36,406
Just rest, okay?

358
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:38,992
- It's just a scratch.
- Hmm.

359
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:43,288
The troll has been caught.

360
00:18:44,414 --> 00:18:46,708
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

361
00:18:46,792 --> 00:18:48,669
His name is Caloy Toledo.

362
00:18:48,752 --> 00:18:49,711
Okay.

363
00:18:50,337 --> 00:18:53,006
However, he doesn't seem to know
who gave the orders.

364
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:56,176
Can't he just describe the person?

365
00:18:56,260 --> 00:18:57,928
What they look like?

366
00:18:58,011 --> 00:18:59,263
Nothing?

367
00:19:00,222 --> 00:19:02,057
He said he never saw them personally.

368
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:05,602
The only way they communicate
is through the messaging app.

369
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:08,689
The payment is left at his door.

370
00:19:08,772 --> 00:19:12,442
The police are checking
if they can see any identity on the app.

371
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:16,905
They are also checking
the CCTV footage in the area.

372
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:18,824
I really hope it's not Val.

373
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:25,581
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

374
00:19:25,664 --> 00:19:26,665
I'm sorry, dude.

375
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:31,128
I'm sorry you got dragged into this mess.

376
00:19:32,129 --> 00:19:33,297
[SIGHS]

377
00:19:34,131 --> 00:19:35,632
What are friends for?

378
00:19:37,926 --> 00:19:39,845
Ouch! [GROANS]

379
00:19:40,429 --> 00:19:41,555
Billy!

380
00:19:41,638 --> 00:19:43,390
- What did you do to me?
- Oh, hush you!

381
00:19:43,473 --> 00:19:44,850
- You're being silly!
- Ouch! Ouch!

382
00:19:44,933 --> 00:19:46,518
- Oh, sorry! [CHUCKLES]
- [CELLPHONE RINGING]

383
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:48,103
I'm sorry!

384
00:19:50,606 --> 00:19:52,649
Oh my God, dude.

385
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:55,319
Oliver's Family Day is tomorrow.

386
00:19:56,028 --> 00:19:57,154
Oh, yeah!

387
00:19:57,946 --> 00:20:00,741
No, I'll explain it to him!

388
00:20:00,824 --> 00:20:02,326
I'll handle it. You rest.

389
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:03,327
I'll take care of it.

390
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:06,538
You should go home.

391
00:20:07,831 --> 00:20:09,416
- I'm fine.
- Are you sure?

392
00:20:09,499 --> 00:20:10,417
Nothing hurts?

393
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:13,003
- Do you need anything else?
- Nope, nothing hurts.

394
00:20:13,086 --> 00:20:14,004
I'm fine.

395
00:20:14,087 --> 00:20:15,756
- I'm okay.
- Let me see.

396
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:17,132
[BOTH YELPS]

397
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:19,927
Just kidding. Call me
if you need anything.

398
00:20:21,261 --> 00:20:22,429
Thanks, dude.

399
00:20:22,512 --> 00:20:28,810
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

400
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:33,732
Good afternoon, everyone!

401
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:35,901
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

402
00:20:35,984 --> 00:20:37,861
[PRINCIPAL] Thank you!

403
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:40,822
Thank you for spending your time today

404
00:20:40,906 --> 00:20:43,492
to celebrate our Family Day!

405
00:20:43,575 --> 00:20:49,331
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

406
00:20:49,414 --> 00:20:51,375
The troll has already been caught.

407
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:54,461
But what if the person who's
paying Caloy has more people?

408
00:20:54,544 --> 00:20:56,088
[PRINCIPAL] And most of all…

409
00:20:56,171 --> 00:20:58,966
Don't worry, Aunt Pres.
I'll hunt them down.

410
00:20:59,049 --> 00:21:01,051
Caloy won't get off either.

411
00:21:01,134 --> 00:21:04,179
I'm getting worried, Billy.

412
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:06,556
[PRINCIPAL] <i>So let's cherish</i>
<i>this moment together.</i>

413
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:08,016
- [OLIVER] Billy! Billy!
- Hmm?

414
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:11,103
Where's Jordan? It's about to start!

415
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:14,773
I'm sorry, but Jordan is injured.

416
00:21:14,856 --> 00:21:16,692
- It's only us today.
- Don't worry about it!

417
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:19,736
- Your sister and I are here!
- See? Present!

418
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:22,531
[PRINCIPAL]
Parents and guardians, welcome!

419
00:21:22,614 --> 00:21:25,909
<i>Let's enjoy the program</i>
<i>and let the games begin!</i>

420
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:30,372
- [CHEERING, APPLAUDING]
- [UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

421
00:21:40,048 --> 00:21:42,342
[CHEERING]

422
00:21:43,844 --> 00:21:48,724
We actually need five trios again
for this game!

423
00:21:48,807 --> 00:21:49,808
We already have two.

424
00:21:49,891 --> 00:21:52,602
Billy! Auntie!
Can we please join this game?

425
00:21:52,686 --> 00:21:54,146
What?

426
00:21:54,229 --> 00:21:56,356
Oh, no, Auntie Pres is injured!

427
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:59,943
Let's just wait for another pairs game,
then we'll win again.

428
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:00,861
I promise, okay?

429
00:22:00,944 --> 00:22:05,532
- There will be more games.
- [TEACHER] We need three more trios!

430
00:22:05,615 --> 00:22:06,825
Hold on!

431
00:22:06,908 --> 00:22:08,535
- We'll join!
- Jordan!

432
00:22:10,078 --> 00:22:12,164
- [JORDAN] Just in time!
- [OLIVER] Yes!

433
00:22:12,247 --> 00:22:14,333
- [PRECIOUS CHUCKLES]
- What is he doing here?

434
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:15,792
You're not supposed to be here!

435
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:18,003
- Please!
- Are you a doctor?

436
00:22:18,086 --> 00:22:19,212
Please?

437
00:22:19,296 --> 00:22:21,882
- [CHUCKLES]
- Hey, little dude.

438
00:22:21,965 --> 00:22:24,009
- Are you ready to win?
- Yes! Super!

439
00:22:24,092 --> 00:22:26,178
- They will all lose to us.
- Yeah, they will.

440
00:22:27,345 --> 00:22:29,056
- ["KULIMLIM" BY ANGELA KEN PLAYING]
- Come on!

441
00:22:29,139 --> 00:22:31,224
Slow down!

442
00:22:32,517 --> 00:22:34,519
[CHEERING]

443
00:22:34,603 --> 00:22:37,481
[OLIVER] Come on! Go!

444
00:22:37,564 --> 00:22:41,651
[INDISTINCT CHATTER, CHEERING]

445
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:43,987
C'mon, Oliver! Do it again!

446
00:22:44,071 --> 00:22:45,781
There! Bite hard!

447
00:22:45,864 --> 00:22:48,158
- C'mon!
- Swallow it!

448
00:22:48,241 --> 00:22:50,077
[BILLY] Good job!

449
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:51,536
[ALL CHEERING]

450
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:55,415
[OLIVER SHOUTING
AND EXCLAIMING EXCITEDLY]

451
00:22:55,499 --> 00:22:56,917
[JORDAN GRUNTS]

452
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,376
- Keep your balance!
- We can do it.

453
00:22:59,169 --> 00:23:01,755
[ONLOOKERS AND CONTESTANTS
EXCLAIM EXCITEDLY]

454
00:23:03,131 --> 00:23:04,633
- Dude.
- Your wound is bleeding!

455
00:23:04,716 --> 00:23:06,718
- C'mon, Billy!
- It's fine!

456
00:23:06,802 --> 00:23:08,887
- C'mon!
- Billy!

457
00:23:08,970 --> 00:23:11,098
- No!
- [JORDAN] Come on!

458
00:23:11,181 --> 00:23:12,766
- Jump!
- Come on, Billy!

459
00:23:12,849 --> 00:23:13,975
Jump!

460
00:23:14,976 --> 00:23:15,852
Are you okay?

461
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:17,187
I'll be fine!

462
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:18,814
[CHEERING]

463
00:23:18,897 --> 00:23:20,273
- Yes!
- We did it!

464
00:23:20,357 --> 00:23:22,067
- We won!
- Wow.

465
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:24,611
Thank you!

466
00:23:24,694 --> 00:23:26,363
[PRINCIPAL] You're welcome!

467
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:28,740
- Ouch!
- [YELPS]

468
00:23:29,616 --> 00:23:30,826
Stop that!

469
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:34,663
You're so stubborn.
I told you not to come.

470
00:23:34,746 --> 00:23:36,498
- Look at what happened!
- I'm fine!

471
00:23:36,581 --> 00:23:39,543
- Your wound was bleeding!
- What's important is that we won!

472
00:23:39,626 --> 00:23:40,794
Okay.

473
00:23:40,877 --> 00:23:44,589
So you feel fine?
Why am I even doing this?

474
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:45,924
[CHUCKLES]

475
00:23:46,633 --> 00:23:48,844
- All done?
- Does it hurt? Hold on, let me fix it.

476
00:23:49,719 --> 00:23:52,097
Hey, by the way,

477
00:23:52,180 --> 00:23:54,307
have you seen my house keys?

478
00:23:54,391 --> 00:23:55,976
I might have left them at your place.

479
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:57,310
Hmm.

480
00:23:58,353 --> 00:23:59,855
I haven't.

481
00:23:59,938 --> 00:24:01,940
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.

482
00:24:02,023 --> 00:24:03,233
Did you lose them?

483
00:24:03,316 --> 00:24:06,319
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

484
00:24:06,403 --> 00:24:07,529
Thanks, dude.

485
00:24:10,615 --> 00:24:17,622
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

486
00:24:30,635 --> 00:24:32,679
[BILLY] Okay, bye, Auntie Pres!

487
00:24:32,762 --> 00:24:34,055
- [OLIVER] Bye!
- [PRECIOUS] Bye!

488
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:35,432
[BILLY] Oliver?

489
00:24:35,932 --> 00:24:38,185
I'll just check on Jordan, okay?

490
00:24:38,268 --> 00:24:40,228
He might be running a fever.
I'll be back soon.

491
00:24:40,312 --> 00:24:41,730
[OLIVER] Do you want me
to go with you?

492
00:24:41,813 --> 00:24:43,690
[BILLY] No, I'll be fine.
Go and shower, then rest.

493
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:46,109
- All right, bye!
- [BILLY] Bye! [SMOOCHES]

494
00:24:46,193 --> 00:24:47,819
Go ahead and shower, okay? You're sweaty!

495
00:24:47,903 --> 00:24:49,321
- Bye, love you!
- I'll be quick, Auntie!

496
00:24:49,404 --> 00:24:51,031
[PRECIOUS] I'll leave your food
in the fridge, okay?

497
00:24:51,114 --> 00:24:54,075
- [BILLY] All right, thank you!
- [PRECIOUS] Okay, bye, take care!

498
00:24:54,159 --> 00:24:55,410
[OLIVER] Bye!

499
00:24:55,493 --> 00:24:57,621
[OLIVER] You were amazing
earlier, Auntie Pres.

500
00:24:57,704 --> 00:25:04,336
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

501
00:25:06,004 --> 00:25:08,381
<i>Are you here</i>
<i>because you're feeling guilty?</i>

502
00:25:08,465 --> 00:25:10,175
<i>Do you really think I would do that?</i>

503
00:25:10,258 --> 00:25:12,886
<i>I'm here because I want to</i>
<i>make it up to Jordan.</i>

504
00:25:12,969 --> 00:25:16,181
<i>We just have to be more prepared</i>
<i>and more careful.</i>

505
00:25:16,264 --> 00:25:17,182
<i>It's nothing.</i>

506
00:25:17,265 --> 00:25:19,100
[VALERIE] <i>I'm doing this for you.</i>

507
00:25:19,184 --> 00:25:21,102
<i>I just wanted to clear the air between us.</i>

508
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:22,520
<i>This caller seems to know you.</i>

509
00:25:22,604 --> 00:25:24,022
<i>How can I support you today?</i>

510
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:26,441
<i>Oh my gosh, Ms. Billy!</i>
<i>Is that really you?</i>

511
00:25:26,524 --> 00:25:28,151
<i>Must be nice.</i>

512
00:25:28,235 --> 00:25:29,778
